:["Q8NBC4"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is thought to be a human-specific protein. Currently available evidence suggests that orthologous regions in other organisms contain sequence differences that would not support production of a protein product. Genome-wide association studies have suggested the possibility that a SNP in the 3' UTR, rs17123507, could be associated with nicotine addiction. Expression of this gene may be elevated in some individuals with Alzheimer's disease. [provided by RefSeq, Mar 2017].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[],"uniprot_source":null,"retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}